        <p>
          One hundred and twenty hours. Broken down, they are just numbers. But lived — they are early mornings, tired muscles, quiet pride, shared laughter, and the slow, steady satisfaction of work done well and done freely.
        </p>
        <p>
          CWTS 2 asked me to give time. What it gave back was far greater: a clearer sense of who I am, a deeper appreciation for community, and a conviction that the most meaningful career I can build is one in service to others. These 120 hours are complete. The lessons they taught me are not.
